 "note": "Dunsborough Tavern, 2 Dunsborough Place, Dunsborough, from the Landgate aerial (Nov 2026) and visitor photos of the beer garden. A big single-storey pub of red face brick, about 54 m by 52 m: a wide hip-roofed main hall with two hipped front wings, a hipped back wing towards Caves Road, all pale grey (Surfmist-like) metal roofs; a brick corner tower with a brown pyramid roof and a glazed lantern over the beer garden; dark timber verandah posts; a square hipped entry porch on the car park side. The beer garden (artificial turf, brick paths, pine tables, white umbrellas, teal and white shade sails) is in front of the hall, facing Dunsborough Place and the car park. Plain lettering, no logo. Metres: x left (south-east, Caves Road end) to right (north-west) as seen from the car park in front (north-east), y back (south-west).",
